IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `clpq-dates`
IMPORT `clpq-claimant`

-- Choice of Law (Limitation Periods) Act 1996 (Queensland) -- worked cases for the claimant's questions
-- (clpq-claimant.l4) and the date helpers (clpq-dates.l4). Every expected value was worked by hand from the deposited
-- text; none was copied from the encoding's output. Each assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not
-- about the law. The facts are illustrative; the periods (3 years, 6 years, 6 months) are inputs standing for whatever
-- the other place's limitation law sets, not statements of that law. The New Zealand declaration taking effect on
-- 1 July 2000 is invented for the cases: whether any declaration has been made is not known from the deposited sources.
-- Day counts used: 3 years from 14 March 2025 ends 14 March 2028; 3 years from 29 February 2024 ends 28 February 2027
-- (2027 has no 29 February: fork F7); 4 years from 29 February 2024 ends 29 February 2028 (2028 is a leap year); 6
-- years from 29 February 2024 ends 28 February 2030; 6 months from 31 August 2025 ends 28 February 2026; 1 year 11
-- months from 31 March 2025 ends 28 February 2027; 10 months from 15 March 2025 ends 15 January 2026.
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `cases`

`d` MEANS `the calendar date`
`State` MEANS `another Australian State (New South Wales, Victoria, South Australia, Tasmania or Western Australia)`
`Territory` MEANS `an Australian Territory (for example the Australian Capital Territory or the Northern Territory)`
`overseas` MEANS `a country other than Australia or New Zealand`
`Qld court` MEANS `a court of Queensland`
`Qld arbitrator` MEANS `an arbitrator, in an arbitration in Queensland`
`elsewhere` MEANS `a court or an arbitrator outside Queensland`

`NZ day` MEANS `d` 1 7 2000
`unused` MEANS `d` 1 1 2000

`nz ok` MEANS `the Act applies to New Zealand law for my proceeding`
`nz undeclared` MEANS `the Act does not apply to New Zealand: no regulation has declared that it applies (s 3(2))`
`nz too early` MEANS `the Act does not apply to my proceeding: it was started before the declaration for New Zealand took effect (s 3(3))`

`reach before` MEANS `yes: the Act applies to my proceeding; my cause of action arose before 1 November 1996, and s 3(1) applies the Act to it`
`reach after` MEANS `yes: the Act applies to my proceeding; my cause of action arose on or after 1 November 1996`
`reach no` MEANS `no: the Act does not apply to a proceeding started before 1 November 1996 (s 3(1))`
`reach no NZ` MEANS `no: New Zealand law governs my claim, and no regulation has declared that the Act applies to New Zealand (s 3(2))`
`reach NZ too early` MEANS `no: New Zealand law governs my claim, and my proceeding was started before the declaration for New Zealand took effect (s 3(3))`

`their law` MEANS `that place's limitation law, as part of the substantive law that governs my claim (s 5)`
`s5 not here` MEANS `s 5 does not apply: my claim is not before a court or an arbitrator of Queensland`
`s5 too early` MEANS `s 5 does not apply: my proceeding was started before 1 November 1996 (s 3(1))`
`s5 NZ undeclared` MEANS `s 5 does not apply: no regulation has declared that the Act applies to New Zealand (s 3(2))`
`s5 NZ too early` MEANS `s 5 does not apply: my proceeding was started before the declaration for New Zealand took effect (s 3(3))`
`s5 Queensland` MEANS `s 5 does not apply: Queensland law governs my claim; Queensland's own limitation law is outside this Act`
`s5 overseas` MEANS `s 5 does not apply: the law of a country other than New Zealand governs my claim; which limitation law applies is outside this Act`

`as there` MEANS `as far as practicable, in the way in which the courts of that place exercise it in comparable cases (s 6)`
`s6 not here` MEANS `s 6 does not apply: the discretion is not exercised by a court or an arbitrator of Queensland`
`s6 too early` MEANS `s 6 does not apply: my proceeding was started before 1 November 1996 (s 3(1))`
`s6 not relevant place` MEANS `s 6 does not apply: the limitation law is not one of a relevant place (another State, a Territory or New Zealand)`
`s6 NZ undeclared` MEANS `s 6 does not apply: no regulation has declared that the Act applies to New Zealand (s 3(2))`
`s6 NZ too early` MEANS `s 6 does not apply: my proceeding was started before the declaration for New Zealand took effect (s 3(3))`
`s6 no discretion` MEANS `s 6 does not apply: that place's limitation law confers no discretion in my case`

`not covered` MEANS `not covered: s 5 does not make another place's limitation law apply to my claim (ask whose limitation law applies)`
`in time` MEANS `yes, in time: I start within that place's limitation period, which the court applies (s 5)`
`late` MEANS `no, out of time under that place's limitation period (s 5), unless the court extends the time under a discretion that law gives, exercised as that place's courts would (s 6)`
`in time extended` MEANS `yes, in time: the court has extended the time under that place's limitation law (s 6), and I start by the extended day`
`late extended` MEANS `no, out of time even as the court extended it under that place's limitation law (s 6)`

§§ `Dates`

#ASSERT `leap year` 2024
#ASSERT `leap year` 2000
#ASSERT NOT (`leap year` 1900)
#ASSERT NOT (`leap year` 2027)
#ASSERT `the number of days in month` 2 `of` 2028 EQUALS 29
#ASSERT `the number of days in month` 2 `of` 2026 EQUALS 28
#ASSERT `the number of days in month` 4 `of` 2026 EQUALS 30
#ASSERT `the number of days in month` 12 `of` 2026 EQUALS 31
#ASSERT `the date` 3 `years and` 0 `months after` (`d` 14 3 2025) EQUALS `d` 14 3 2028
#ASSERT `the date` 3 `years and` 0 `months after` (`d` 29 2 2024) EQUALS `d` 28 2 2027
#ASSERT `the date` 4 `years and` 0 `months after` (`d` 29 2 2024) EQUALS `d` 29 2 2028
#ASSERT `the date` 6 `years and` 0 `months after` (`d` 29 2 2024) EQUALS `d` 28 2 2030
#ASSERT `the date` 0 `years and` 6 `months after` (`d` 31 8 2025) EQUALS `d` 28 2 2026
#ASSERT `the date` 1 `years and` 11 `months after` (`d` 31 3 2025) EQUALS `d` 28 2 2027
#ASSERT `the date` 0 `years and` 10 `months after` (`d` 15 3 2025) EQUALS `d` 15 1 2026
#ASSERT `the date` 0 `years and` 0 `months after` (`d` 15 3 2025) EQUALS `d` 15 3 2025
#ASSERT `the days from` (`d` 14 3 2025) `to` (`d` 14 3 2028) EQUALS 1096

§§ `The facts the Act turns on`

#ASSERT `s 4 -- a relevant place` `State`
#ASSERT `s 4 -- a relevant place` `Territory`
#ASSERT `s 4 -- a relevant place` `New Zealand`
#ASSERT NOT (`s 4 -- a relevant place` `Queensland`)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 4 -- a relevant place` `overseas`)
#ASSERT `ss 4, 5, 6 -- a court of the State` `Qld court`
#ASSERT `ss 4, 5, 6 -- a court of the State` `Qld arbitrator`
#ASSERT NOT (`ss 4, 5, 6 -- a court of the State` `elsewhere`)

§§ `s 4 -- what a limitation law is`

-- "An action may not be brought after 3 years": both limbs.
#ASSERT `Is this a limitation law` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A notice of claim to be given within 6 months: bars the claim, but not by the time a proceeding is started.
#ASSERT `Is this a limitation law` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Is this a limitation law` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Is this a limitation law` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `ss 3(2), 3(3) -- New Zealand`

#ASSERT `ss 3(2), 3(3) -- New Zealand` FALSE `unused` (`d` 7 11 2026) EQUALS `nz undeclared`
#ASSERT `ss 3(2), 3(3) -- New Zealand` TRUE `NZ day` (`d` 30 6 2000) EQUALS `nz too early`
#ASSERT `ss 3(2), 3(3) -- New Zealand` TRUE `NZ day` (`d` 1 7 2000) EQUALS `nz ok`
#ASSERT `ss 3(2), 3(3) -- New Zealand` TRUE `NZ day` (`d` 7 11 2026) EQUALS `nz ok`

§§ `ss 2, 3 -- whether the Act reaches my proceeding`

#ASSERT `Does the Act reach my proceeding` (`d` 1 1 1990) (`d` 31 10 1996) `State` FALSE `unused` EQUALS `reach no`
#ASSERT `Does the Act reach my proceeding` (`d` 1 1 1990) (`d` 1 11 1996) `State` FALSE `unused` EQUALS `reach before`
#ASSERT `Does the Act reach my proceeding` (`d` 31 10 1996) (`d` 1 12 1997) `State` FALSE `unused` EQUALS `reach before`
#ASSERT `Does the Act reach my proceeding` (`d` 1 11 1996) (`d` 1 12 1997) `State` FALSE `unused` EQUALS `reach after`
#ASSERT `Does the Act reach my proceeding` (`d` 14 3 2025) (`d` 7 11 2026) `Territory` FALSE `unused` EQUALS `reach after`
-- New Zealand law governs.
#ASSERT `Does the Act reach my proceeding` (`d` 14 3 2025) (`d` 7 11 2026) `New Zealand` FALSE `unused` EQUALS `reach no NZ`
#ASSERT `Does the Act reach my proceeding` (`d` 1 1 2000) (`d` 30 6 2000) `New Zealand` TRUE `NZ day` EQUALS `reach NZ too early`
#ASSERT `Does the Act reach my proceeding` (`d` 1 1 2000) (`d` 1 7 2000) `New Zealand` TRUE `NZ day` EQUALS `reach after`
-- A cause of action arising before the commencement, sued on after the NZ declaration: s 3(3) bars only earlier proceedings.
#ASSERT `Does the Act reach my proceeding` (`d` 1 1 1995) (`d` 1 7 2000) `New Zealand` TRUE `NZ day` EQUALS `reach before`
-- Started before the commencement: s 3(1) answers first.
#ASSERT `Does the Act reach my proceeding` (`d` 1 1 1995) (`d` 31 10 1996) `New Zealand` FALSE `unused` EQUALS `reach no`
-- The New Zealand facts do not matter for another State.
#ASSERT `Does the Act reach my proceeding` (`d` 14 3 2025) (`d` 7 11 2026) `State` TRUE `NZ day` EQUALS `reach after`

§§ `s 5 -- whose limitation law the court applies`

-- Injured in another State, sued in a Queensland court: that State's limitation law.
#ASSERT `Whose limitation law applies to my claim` `Qld court` `State` (`d` 7 11 2026) FALSE `unused` EQUALS `their law`
#ASSERT `Whose limitation law applies to my claim` `Qld court` `Territory` (`d` 7 11 2026) FALSE `unused` EQUALS `their law`
#ASSERT `Whose limitation law applies to my claim` `Qld arbitrator` `State` (`d` 7 11 2026) FALSE `unused` EQUALS `their law`
#ASSERT `Whose limitation law applies to my claim` `Qld court` `Queensland` (`d` 7 11 2026) FALSE `unused` EQUALS `s5 Queensland`
#ASSERT `Whose limitation law applies to my claim` `Qld court` `overseas` (`d` 7 11 2026) FALSE `unused` EQUALS `s5 overseas`
#ASSERT `Whose limitation law applies to my claim` `elsewhere` `State` (`d` 7 11 2026) FALSE `unused` EQUALS `s5 not here`
#ASSERT `Whose limitation law applies to my claim` `elsewhere` `New Zealand` (`d` 7 11 2026) TRUE `NZ day` EQUALS `s5 not here`
#ASSERT `Whose limitation law applies to my claim` `Qld court` `State` (`d` 31 10 1996) FALSE `unused` EQUALS `s5 too early`
#ASSERT `Whose limitation law applies to my claim` `Qld court` `State` (`d` 1 11 1996) FALSE `unused` EQUALS `their law`
-- New Zealand.
#ASSERT `Whose limitation law applies to my claim` `Qld court` `New Zealand` (`d` 7 11 2026) FALSE `unused` EQUALS `s5 NZ undeclared`
#ASSERT `Whose limitation law applies to my claim` `Qld court` `New Zealand` (`d` 30 6 2000) TRUE `NZ day` EQUALS `s5 NZ too early`
#ASSERT `Whose limitation law applies to my claim` `Qld court` `New Zealand` (`d` 1 7 2000) TRUE `NZ day` EQUALS `their law`
#ASSERT `Whose limitation law applies to my claim` `Qld arbitrator` `New Zealand` (`d` 7 11 2026) TRUE `NZ day` EQUALS `their law`

§§ `s 6 -- how a discretion under that limitation law is used`

#ASSERT `How will the court use a discretion under that law` `Qld court` `State` TRUE (`d` 7 11 2026) FALSE `unused` EQUALS `as there`
#ASSERT `How will the court use a discretion under that law` `Qld arbitrator` `Territory` TRUE (`d` 7 11 2026) FALSE `unused` EQUALS `as there`
#ASSERT `How will the court use a discretion under that law` `Qld court` `Territory` TRUE (`d` 1 11 1996) FALSE `unused` EQUALS `as there`
#ASSERT `How will the court use a discretion under that law` `Qld court` `State` FALSE (`d` 7 11 2026) FALSE `unused` EQUALS `s6 no discretion`
#ASSERT `How will the court use a discretion under that law` `Qld court` `Queensland` TRUE (`d` 7 11 2026) FALSE `unused` EQUALS `s6 not relevant place`
#ASSERT `How will the court use a discretion under that law` `Qld court` `overseas` TRUE (`d` 7 11 2026) FALSE `unused` EQUALS `s6 not relevant place`
#ASSERT `How will the court use a discretion under that law` `elsewhere` `State` TRUE (`d` 7 11 2026) FALSE `unused` EQUALS `s6 not here`
#ASSERT `How will the court use a discretion under that law` `Qld court` `State` TRUE (`d` 31 10 1996) FALSE `unused` EQUALS `s6 too early`
#ASSERT `How will the court use a discretion under that law` `Qld court` `New Zealand` TRUE (`d` 7 11 2026) FALSE `unused` EQUALS `s6 NZ undeclared`
#ASSERT `How will the court use a discretion under that law` `Qld court` `New Zealand` TRUE (`d` 30 6 2000) TRUE `NZ day` EQUALS `s6 NZ too early`
#ASSERT `How will the court use a discretion under that law` `Qld court` `New Zealand` TRUE (`d` 1 7 2000) TRUE `NZ day` EQUALS `as there`
#ASSERT `How will the court use a discretion under that law` `Qld court` `New Zealand` FALSE (`d` 1 7 2000) TRUE `NZ day` EQUALS `s6 no discretion`

§§ `ss 5, 6 -- the rule with its deadline`

#ASSERT `started in time under` (`s 5 -- start within that place's limitation period` 10) `at` 0
#ASSERT `started in time under` (`s 5 -- start within that place's limitation period` 10) `at` 10
#ASSERT NOT (`started in time under` (`s 5 -- start within that place's limitation period` 10) `at` 11)
#ASSERT `started by the last day` (`d` 1 6 2026) (`d` 1 6 2029) (`d` 1 5 2026)

§§ `ss 5, 6 -- am I in time under that place's limitation law`

-- Injured in another State on 14 March 2025; that State's law gives 3 years from that day; sued in a Queensland court.
#ASSERT `Am I in time under that place's limitation law` `Qld court` `State` FALSE `unused` 3 0 (`d` 14 3 2025) FALSE `unused` (`d` 13 3 2028) EQUALS `in time`
#ASSERT `Am I in time under that place's limitation law` `Qld court` `State` FALSE `unused` 3 0 (`d` 14 3 2025) FALSE `unused` (`d` 14 3 2028) EQUALS `in time`
#ASSERT `Am I in time under that place's limitation law` `Qld court` `State` FALSE `unused` 3 0 (`d` 14 3 2025) FALSE `unused` (`d` 15 3 2028) EQUALS `late`
#ASSERT `Am I in time under that place's limitation law` `Qld court` `State` FALSE `unused` 3 0 (`d` 14 3 2025) FALSE `unused` (`d` 14 3 2025) EQUALS `in time`
-- The court extended the time to 30 June 2028 under that State's law.
#ASSERT `Am I in time under that place's limitation law` `Qld court` `State` FALSE `unused` 3 0 (`d` 14 3 2025) TRUE (`d` 30 6 2028) (`d` 15 3 2028) EQUALS `in time extended`
#ASSERT `Am I in time under that place's limitation law` `Qld court` `State` FALSE `unused` 3 0 (`d` 14 3 2025) TRUE (`d` 30 6 2028) (`d` 30 6 2028) EQUALS `in time extended`
#ASSERT `Am I in time under that place's limitation law` `Qld court` `State` FALSE `unused` 3 0 (`d` 14 3 2025) TRUE (`d` 30 6 2028) (`d` 1 7 2028) EQUALS `late extended`
-- 29 February start, 3 years: the last day is 28 February 2027 (fork F7).
#ASSERT `Am I in time under that place's limitation law` `Qld court` `Territory` FALSE `unused` 3 0 (`d` 29 2 2024) FALSE `unused` (`d` 28 2 2027) EQUALS `in time`
#ASSERT `Am I in time under that place's limitation law` `Qld court` `Territory` FALSE `unused` 3 0 (`d` 29 2 2024) FALSE `unused` (`d` 1 3 2027) EQUALS `late`
-- A period of 6 months from 31 August 2025, before an arbitrator in Queensland under New Zealand law, declared.
#ASSERT `Am I in time under that place's limitation law` `Qld arbitrator` `New Zealand` TRUE `NZ day` 0 6 (`d` 31 8 2025) FALSE `unused` (`d` 28 2 2026) EQUALS `in time`
#ASSERT `Am I in time under that place's limitation law` `Qld arbitrator` `New Zealand` TRUE `NZ day` 0 6 (`d` 31 8 2025) FALSE `unused` (`d` 1 3 2026) EQUALS `late`
-- The same, with no declaration for New Zealand: s 5 does not apply.
#ASSERT `Am I in time under that place's limitation law` `Qld arbitrator` `New Zealand` FALSE `unused` 0 6 (`d` 31 8 2025) FALSE `unused` (`d` 28 2 2026) EQUALS `not covered`
-- Started before the period runs (fork F8).
#ASSERT `Am I in time under that place's limitation law` `Qld court` `State` FALSE `unused` 3 0 (`d` 1 6 2026) FALSE `unused` (`d` 1 5 2026) EQUALS `in time`
-- A period of no length: the last day is the day it runs from.
#ASSERT `Am I in time under that place's limitation law` `Qld court` `State` FALSE `unused` 0 0 (`d` 1 6 2026) FALSE `unused` (`d` 1 6 2026) EQUALS `in time`
#ASSERT `Am I in time under that place's limitation law` `Qld court` `State` FALSE `unused` 0 0 (`d` 1 6 2026) FALSE `unused` (`d` 2 6 2026) EQUALS `late`
-- s 5 does not apply.
#ASSERT `Am I in time under that place's limitation law` `Qld court` `Queensland` FALSE `unused` 3 0 (`d` 14 3 2025) FALSE `unused` (`d` 13 3 2028) EQUALS `not covered`
#ASSERT `Am I in time under that place's limitation law` `Qld court` `overseas` FALSE `unused` 3 0 (`d` 14 3 2025) FALSE `unused` (`d` 13 3 2028) EQUALS `not covered`
#ASSERT `Am I in time under that place's limitation law` `elsewhere` `State` FALSE `unused` 3 0 (`d` 14 3 2025) FALSE `unused` (`d` 13 3 2028) EQUALS `not covered`
#ASSERT `Am I in time under that place's limitation law` `Qld court` `State` FALSE `unused` 3 0 (`d` 1 1 1994) FALSE `unused` (`d` 31 10 1996) EQUALS `not covered`
#ASSERT `Am I in time under that place's limitation law` `Qld court` `State` FALSE `unused` 3 0 (`d` 1 1 1994) FALSE `unused` (`d` 1 11 1996) EQUALS `in time`

§§ `ss 5, 6 -- by when must I start`

